---
import Header from "~/components/Header.astro";
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Header demo" noIndex>
	<Header slot="header" active="home" count={247} />

	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
		<p class="font-display text-kicker tracking-kicker text-ink-3 uppercase">demo</p>
		<h1 class="font-display text-h1 tracking-display mt-2">Site header</h1>
		<p class="text-body text-ink-2 mt-4 max-w-prose">
			Live render of <code>~/components/Header.astro</code>. Top of page is the non-sticky look
			(72px desktop, 56px mobile, transparent). Scroll any distance to trigger the sticky state:
			blurred paper background, 60px height on desktop, soft drop shadow. Resize to a narrow
			viewport to swap the nav and Share CTA for the hamburger.
		</p>

		<h2 class="font-display text-h2 tracking-display mt-12">Checks</h2>
		<ul class="text-body text-ink-2 mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
			<li>
				Active nav item (<code>Home</code>) shows the ink colour, semibold weight, and the amber
				underline.
			</li>
			<li>The voice counter dot pulses (held still under reduced-motion).</li>
			<li>Tab order: skip link → wordmark → nav links → Share button → page content.</li>
			<li>Hamburger button is a placeholder; the drawer is a follow-up issue.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 class="font-display text-h2 tracking-display mt-12">Sticky preview</h2>
		<p class="text-body text-ink-2 mt-4 max-w-prose">
			The header below has its sticky look forced via the <code>sticky</code> prop, so the look can be
			eyeballed without scrolling. It also stands in for the squad/letter pages, which ship with the compact
			treatment locked from the top.
		</p>
		<div class="border-rule mt-6 border">
			<Header active="letter" count={247} sticky />
			<div class="bg-paper p-12">
				<p class="text-caption text-ink-3">
					Page content would begin here; the sticky-locked header sits above this surface.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2 class="font-display text-h2 tracking-display mt-12">Scroll target</h2>
		<p class="text-body text-ink-2 mt-4 max-w-prose">
			A tall block so the page can scroll. The sticky behaviour above should engage once you've
			scrolled a few pixels.
		</p>
		<div class="bg-paper-2 mt-8 h-[200vh] rounded" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
